@bendrucker That's a good direction definitely. 
It would be lovely to see some way to get `terraform validate` to ignore required fields which can be configured in the ENV. I don't see any particular purpose to expose my AWS credentials to `terraform validate`. Sure, I could populate them with bogus values, but that just a hacky workaround. Something like setting the value in the provider config `aws_credentials_id = fromEnv`. Which would stop `validate` from complaining and wouldn't require me to expose secrets.

It would also be great notation for actually documenting how our providers are configured for new people :)

@pselle The team that maintains the `azurerm` provider has been tracking this issue: https://github.com/terraform-providers/terraform-provider-azurerm/issues/7359

I was just wondering if you knew - since this issue has now been merged/closed, when can we expect it to be released?

cc @manicminer @tombuildsstuff - Is there anything else that needs to be done on the `azurerm` side?
